.TH CYAML_SERIALIZE_FREE_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_serialize_free_mp, cyaml_serialize_free \- free a serializer buffer
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

void cyaml_serialize_free_mp(char *s, ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp);
void cyaml_serialize_free(char *s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Free a buffer returned by cyaml_serialize() or cyaml_serialize_flow().
cyaml_serialize_free() is an inline wrapper that passes NULL for mp.

The mp argument must match the allocator that was active when the DOM
tree was created (i.e., the mp passed to cyaml_parse_mp() or the
create functions).  Passing the wrong allocator is undefined behaviour.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s    String to free.  May be NULL (no-op).
mp   Allocator to use for deallocation, or NULL for the default.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_serialize (3),
.BR cyaml_serialize_flow (3)
